# Skill auto-router (mandatory)

Before substantive work, match the task below and **Read** the listed `.cursor/skills/*/SKILL.md` files, then follow them. Do not skip because you “already know” the skill.

## By file / path (also enforced by glob rules)

| Working in… | Read skills |
|-------------|-------------|
| `apps/backend/**/*.cs`, `*.csproj` | `dotnet-modular-monolith`, `dotnet-clean-code`, `semantic-naming` (new names) |
| `apps/desktop/**`, `**/src-tauri/**`, Tauri/`*.rs` desktop host | `rust-tauri`, `rust-security`; + `rust-architecture` if crates/structure; + `rust-fundamentals` if language/async/errors; handbook via `rust-tauri-handbook` when scaffolding or setting standards |
| `apps/web` operator (`orders`, `logistics`, `inventory`, `warehouse`, `pos`, `login`) | `react-best-practices`, `composition-patterns` |
| Public / marketing UI (`(public)`, landing, pricing, signup, onboarding) | `taste`, `ui-ux-pro`, `marketing-copy`; `cro` / `growth-seo` if conversion or SEO |
| `packages/types`, `packages/events`, `packages/sdk`, Prisma schema, new commands/events/DTOs | `semantic-naming` |
| `docs/**`, ADRs, domain pages, Notion sync of docs | `stop-slop`, `doc-coauthoring`, `notion-docs-sync` |
| New product initiative / plan / checkpoint (post-migration) | Name capability first; follow `product-initiatives` rule — not `docs/migration/` |
| Playwright / E2E specs | `webapp-testing` |
| `apps/mobile` or RN | `react-native`; store listing → `aso` |
| MCP server / tools | `mcp-server-patterns`, `mcp-builder` |

## By intent (user words / situation)

| Signal | Read skills |
|--------|-------------|
| Bug, broken, failing, regression, “diagnose” | `diagnose` (+ `tdd` if fixing with tests) |
| “TDD”, red-green-refactor, test-first | `tdd` |
| Vague / underspecified request | `prompt-improver` before coding |
| Architecture deepen / seams / extract | `improve-codebase-architecture` |
| “grill me”, challenge plan, high-stakes decision | `grill-me` (+ `grill-with-docs` if domain docs matter) |
| PRD / issues / triage | `to-prd` / `to-issues` / `triage` |
| Onboard / learn codebase / prime context | `learn-codebase` (+ `graphify` queries) |
| Cross-file “how does X connect” | `graphify` (rule already always-on) |
| Long session / losing context / handoff | `context-hygiene`, `handoff` |
| Design / redesign / polish / critique UI | `impeccable` (+ `taste` if public) |
| Tracking, KPIs, dashboards | `analytics` |
| SMS / push / WhatsApp / notifications | `messaging` |
| Export PDF/XLSX/invoice/manifest | `documents` |
| Pricing / packaging / Stripe tiers | `pricing` |
| Commit/PR prose, changelog, human text | `stop-slop` |
| Spec-kit / large unclear slice | `spec-kit` or `ecc` as appropriate |
| Commit hooks / Husky setup | `setup-pre-commit` |
| Rust/Tauri review, desktop PR review | `rust-code-review` (+ `rust-security`) |
| SQLite / local cache / offline sync in desktop | `rust-sqlite`, `rust-architecture` |
| Tauri binary size, IPC jank, startup | `rust-tauri-performance` |
| Tauri bundle / updater / signing | `rust-tauri-deployment` |
| Desktop window/tray/POS UX chrome | `desktop-ux` |
| Rust+Tauri handbook / standards / scaffold | `rust-tauri-handbook` |

## Explicit-only (never auto)

Only when the user invokes them: `caveman`, `zoom-out`, `write-a-skill`, `web-artifacts`, `prototype`, `understand-anything`, `claude-mem` (unless search cost is clearly high).

## Conflict resolution

1. Path rules win for code under that path.
2. If both public and operator UI: use the surface being edited.
3. Backend C# always beats generic TS/Nest advice still lingering in old docs.
4. Desktop Tauri (`apps/desktop`) beats generic Electron/web advice; Rust host skills beat frontend-only patterns for IPC/secrets/hardware.
5. Prefer reading the skill over inventing parallel conventions.
